    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d669">

                <pb facs="0889" n="775" xml:id="pg775"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.6363/54: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Genoa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-04T09:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1922—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 4—5:57 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Your telegram of May 2, 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">4</hi>] p.m. I have a
                    categorical denial from Worthington-Evans<anchor n="16" xml:id="d669-f1"/> that
                    the supposed Krassin, Boyle, Dutch-Shell agreement has been signed. Evans states
                    that the information would have been given to his delegation if it were true. In
                    answer to an inquirer the Russian delegation has replied that while negotiations
                    have been taking place a conclusion has not been reached.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d669-f1" n="16" xml:id="d669-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Laming Worthington-Evans, member of the British delegation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
